{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>ותראני האתון.</b> With kamatz gadol in place of patach, for it should have been ותראני. Many are like this. Perhaps it is divided for many reasons, and here it is like לולא ('were it not'). And the word גם means forever, until the donkey died after she spoke." "<b>ואותה החייתי.</b> Shortened form. And likewise the meaning: had I killed her, I would have killed you; or I would have killed you alone, and her I kept alive." "And the meaning of <b>ואותה החייתי</b> is: a human being, upon seeing the angel, would die — and the proof is 'and my soul was saved'; and Manoah said so too. How much more so the beast, which has no partnership whatsoever with the spirit of the angel, unlike a human being."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:03.405659414Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}